      "message": "fix(posting): the index swing judges the swept work against the standing steel\n\nAs a work-turning A indexes, the stock, parts and turning fixtures it\nsweeps are now judged against the face the rotary stands on (the machine\nfile's new axis_to_table, its centre height; the microARC 4 states\n3.15 in) and against every fixed fixture over the work's X span, by its\nbox's distance from the line. A strike refuses the post naming the op,\nthe index and the steel; a machine with no figure, a fixture with no\nfacets or one reaching across the line is named in the gate's\nnot-judged line, never skipped in silence.\n\nFixes #1107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
